<title>BULGARIA: Yield falls to 0.69 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls to 0.69 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield fell further on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Wednesday as the issue was oversubscribed two-fold, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity on the issue was 0.69 percent, down from 0.72 percent on Tuesday, 0.78 percent at Monday's auction and 0.90 percent on Friday, figures showed.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with a par value of 15 billion levs and no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3039297000</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     15,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 19</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 17</p>
<p> Bids received		 30,603 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   99.28 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 15,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  99.31 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     0.69 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
